-- title:
--   Degeneracy embeddings and pinned level-M/p generic fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$ but $p^2\nmid M$, a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, with $M/p\neq 0$, and assume `jqModC ℚ` lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $SL(2,\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` (a Deligne–Rapoport-type integral model package at level $\Gamma_M$, carrying a forgetful morphism $\mathfrak{X}.\pi$ to the level-$\Gamma_N$ two-chart model, an isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.w$, and a pinned curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ of the geometric generic fibre over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). Let $\theta$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` such that whenever an element of that field and an element $u$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` have the same underlying Laurent series, the image under $\theta$ has Laurent series `qExpand _ p u`, i.e. $u(q^p)$; and assume $\theta$ reads $\mathfrak{X}.w$ on places: for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y,y'$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base, if $y'$ transported by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection and then followed by $\mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom}$ agrees with the corresponding transport of $y$, then the place attached to $y'$ is `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut θ` applied to the place attached to $y$. The conclusion asserts the existence of two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra maps $\alpha_H,\beta_H$ from `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` to `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` whose underlying ring homomorphisms are integral, with $\alpha_H$ preserving Laurent series, $\beta_H u$ having Laurent series `qExpand _ p u`, together with a curve model $\mathrm{Meta}_0$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with its function field identified with that field and its closed points in bijection with places) and an isomorphism $e_0$ from $\mathrm{Meta}_0.C$ onto the fibre product of the level-$\Gamma_N$ two-chart model `toBase p (XHDRLevel.ΓN p M H hpM) hj` with $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}(R\,p)$, such that: $e_0$ followed by the second projection is $\mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{toBase}$; for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ and $y_0$ of $\mathrm{Meta}_0.C$ whose images in the level-$\Gamma_N$ model agree after composing $y$ with $\mathfrak{X}.\pi.1$ (respectively with $\mathfrak{X}.w.\mathrm{hom}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\pi.1$), the place of $y_0$ is the restriction along $\alpha_H$ (respectively $\beta_H$), i.e. the comap of the valuation subring, of the place of $y$; and finally the preimage under $e_0$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite chart is nonempty and pins $\mathrm{Meta}_0$: for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin p (XHDRLevel.ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, the element of the level-$(M/p)$ field obtained by pulling $a$ back through that open immersion, taking the germ at the generic point and applying $\mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, has underlying Laurent series equal to `coeffEmb` applied to the $q$-expansion of $a$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre dictionary at a prime exactly dividing the level: it produces the two degeneracy embeddings of function fields, $q\mapsto q$ and $q\mapsto q^p$, identifies the geometric generic fibre of the level-$(M/p)$ model as a curve model whose places are the restrictions of places upstairs along those embeddings, and in addition fixes the chosen isomorphism by pinning the $q$-expansions of the finite-chart functions. It is used in the construction of level data and the Picard-group dictionary for the Néron model of $J_H$ at $p$.
